// activediq.connector.v1 — VerifyConnection (contract v1.1, T-0091; v1.2, T-0122).
//
// The connector's own rights check, run as the connector identity (TM §6.5 for AD, §6.6
// "Verification" for Entra). It answers DM-24 (ConnectionVerification) and is the only source of
// the connector's write gate: Plan and Apply refuse with ERROR_CODE_ACTIVATION_REFUSED_OVERPRIVILEGED
// unless the connector's latest run for the connection opens it (contract §8.2).
//
// The response streams: findings are bounded by the Tier-0 set and the managed OU count (DM-24.I7),
// which can exceed one message. A result is valid only if the stream ends with
// VerificationCompleted (contract §2 rule 11).
//
// Findings hold identifiers, not names (DM-24.I3). They enumerate the forest's Tier-0 exposure, so
// the server stores them under FR-16 access rules and never copies an identifier into an audit
// event (DM-24.I5).

